-- M4-4B: durable duplicate protection for article prose extraction. The
-- extraction persists its result as one `article_statements` claim on the
-- article's URL entity; this partial unique index makes a second such claim
-- for the same evidence structurally impossible, so a concurrent worker or a
-- redelivery cannot write it twice (the in-process check-then-act alone could
-- not guarantee this). Generated by drizzle-kit from src/schema/evidence.ts.
-- Forward-only and additive: it constrains only claims whose attribute is
-- 'article_statements', an attribute no existing row carries, so the build
-- touches nothing already stored. Built as plain CREATE UNIQUE INDEX, like
-- every index migration here: the migrator runs in a transaction, where
-- CONCURRENTLY is not allowed.
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "claims_one_article_statements_per_evidence" ON "claims" USING btree ("tenant_id","evidence_id","attribute") WHERE "attribute" = 'article_statements';
